name vis-cloud-1
timeout 200

# THROUGH A CLOUD DECK -- the price doc/sensors.md §6.5 named for the IRST and declined, and the one
# this channel pays: a MARCH along the line of sight through core/FBCloudDensity for a real
# transmittance, instead of the lid a broken deck is to the KOLS.
#
#     T_cloud = exp( -sum sigma_deck * rho * ds )
#
# with the per-deck extinction the cloud stage already publishes (0.022 / 0.018 / 0.0060 1/m at
# density 1) and rho the SAME closed-form field the renderer draws -- one function, two evaluators.
# T multiplies the contrast in the same currency as the Koschmieder haze term, so nothing new is
# calibrated. The march is bounded by the eye's own reach: at most three shell segments, a path of a few
# km, <= 8 contacts at 1 Hz.
#
# THE CONTROL AND THE CASE ARE IN THE SAME RUN, UNDER THE SAME SKY:
#
#   under   3 km ahead at the observer's own altitude, 100 kt slower -- the whole line of sight stays
#           BELOW the deck base. It is seen normally, and its detection range is what this air's
#           visibility is worth.
#   over    crossing left to right 1350 m HIGHER, so its line of sight climbs through the deck. It is
#           inside the +-60/+-40 cone throughout and its presented dimension is the LARGER one (a side
#           view, 14.6 m against 9.14) -- everything is in its favour except the cloud.
#
# `wx fixture` is the committed GFS blob; over this corridor the 2026-07-27T00Z cycle reports ~49-53 %
# low cloud with a ceiling near 2 980 m, which core/FBCloudDensity turns into one deck of roughly
# 2 977 ... 3 877 m. The observer flies at 2 600 m, under it, and `over` at 3 950 m, above it.
#
# MEASURED, AND IT CONTRADICTS THE REASON THE MARCH WAS BOUGHT. doc/sensors.md §9.6c argued that a lid
# OVER-reports blindness because "a 40 % deck is mostly hole". Over the whole fixture the opposite holds:
# rays with T > 0.1 are 100 % below 20 % cover, 32.6 % at 30-40 %, and **0 % at 40-50 %** -- 900 m of
# deck at 0.022 /m closes any ray that crosses it. So at THIS cell's ~50 % cover the lid rule
# (kCloudMaskCover 0.5) sits exactly on the fence while the march reports optical depth 22.5. The march
# is still the right model; the band in which it differs from a lid is 20-50 %, and there it is
# STRICTER, not more permissive. That finding is in the file's Gaps, not hidden here.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   vis_masked        counts contacts this frame that the CLOUD TRANSMITTANCE rejected -- i.e. that
#                     would have been detected in the same air with a clear line of sight. It is only
#                     tallied where the cloud is what decided the outcome, never for a target that was
#                     never going to be seen anyway.
#   events.log        `vis CONTACT` for `under`, `vis MASKED` for `over` with the subtense it had
#   telemetry         vis_contacts never counts `over`
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the verdict AND the pass. A measurement rig, not a task.

wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb
time 2026-06-21T11:00:00Z

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.60000 6.90000 2600 0.0 300          # under the deck
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.95932 6.90000 2600 300

unit under
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.62695 6.89673 2600 0.0 200          # 3 km ahead, co-altitude: no cloud on the line of sight
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.95932 6.89673 2600 200

unit over
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.68085 6.81634 3950 90.0 300         # crossing, 1350 m higher: the line of sight cuts the deck
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.68085 7.21378 3950 300
